==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|freġnan}}, {{l|ang|frīnan}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*fregnaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*preḱ-||to ask}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|fregnan}}, {{cog|non|fregna}}, {{cog|got|𐍆𐍂𐌰𐌹𐌷𐌽𐌰𐌽}}, and related to {{cog|goh|frāga}} ({{cog|de|Frage}}). The Indo-European root also gave {{cog|peo|𐎠𐎱𐎼𐎿𐎶||tr=aparsam|I asked}}, {{cog|sga|arcaid}}, {{cog|wlm|archaf}}, {{cog|xcl|հարց}}, {{cog|xto|prak-}}, {{cog|txb|prek-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfrijnɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|head=friġnan}}

# to [[ask]], [[pray]]

